title: "Collatz basin densities, Fourier decay, and Syracuse integrability: papers and Lean proofs"
authors:
  - family-names: Valbuena
    given-names: Lucas
repository-code: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
url: "https://github.com/x1xhlol/collatz-two-coordinate-obstruction"
abstract: >-
  Three papers with Lean proofs. The Syracuse-law paper proves a quadratic
  upper bound for full-Haar cylinder energy and a normalized stationary
  density whose exact real Lp range is 1 <= p < 2. The affine-law paper
  proves primitive Fourier decay uniform in a growing conductor deficit
  and affine seed, including polynomial-mass total-exponent conditioning
  and the central slice. The basin paper proves uniform inverse-linear
  predecessor density bounds, a finite-energy criterion for universal
  eventual periodicity, a raw occupation lower bound and divergent excess,
  and an almost-sure inverse height clock. Each proof bundle states its
  fresh-check and dependency-reuse scope. The Collatz conjecture remains open.
keywords:
  - Collatz conjecture
  - predecessor density
  - natural density
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - canonical traces
  - Fourier decay
  - Syracuse affine laws
  - Subspace Theorem
  - 3-adic probability
  - integrability
